\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Placement radius of every LIBERO task, computed from the shipped initial states alone --- no policy, no simulator, no training. The last column counts tasks whose identity-bearing object a single constant serves at the tolerance we measure for this controller (\S  \ref {sec:refute}). \textbf  {LIBERO-Object pins all ten of the objects its tasks are individuated by; elsewhere two of thirty}, and $^\dagger $both of those are the fixture tasks --- a drawer and a stove --- which have $R = 0$ because they are bolted down, not because a randomisable placement was frozen. \emph  {No} suite is admissible on the shared container, LIBERO-Object included. Artifact: \texttt  {results/admissibility.json}.}}{3}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
